# :scanner instrumentation suite on a physical Android 15 device.
#
# The README had carried "Verified on a physical Android 15 or 16 device" as an open item
# since Phase 2, for the honest reason that no such device existed here. One does now: a
# Xiaomi 25010PN30C (xuanyuan), Android 15 / API 35, SM8550, arm64-v8a, reached through the
# webcontrol root agent rather than adb -- no ADB listener was opened on this phone.
#
# How it was run, so it can be run again:
#   ./gradlew :scanner:assembleDebugAndroidTest
#   # strip the ABIs the phone does not have, so the transfer is 6 MB instead of 12:
#   zip -d <apk> 'lib/x86_64/*' 'lib/armeabi-v7a/*' && apksigner sign --ks ~/.android/debug.keystore ...
#   # ship it to the phone through the control channel and install:
#   ctl /push {"path":"/data/local/tmp/zxing-at.apk","data":"<base64>"}
#   ctl /exec pm install -t -r -g /data/local/tmp/zxing-at.apk
#   ctl /exec am instrument -w io.github.kakakakacat.zxing.android.scanner.test/androidx.test.runner.AndroidJUnitRunner
#
# One thing this does NOT prove: 16 KB page support. getconf PAGE_SIZE on this device is
# 4096, so the loader never had to honour the 16 KB alignment the AAR is built with. What it
# does prove is that libzxingnative.so loads and decodes on real Android 15 hardware.
#
# What the suite covers is in HANDOFF.md; the 21 tests are 35 fixed frames over 16 formats,
# a live format-switch test, the default-backend checks and the native backend.
#
# fingerprint / soc / page size, then the run:
#
Xiaomi/xuanyuan/xuanyuan:15/AQ3A.240912.001/OS2.0.207.0.VOACNXM:user/release-keys
